Let vLLM INC serve a GPTQ-quantized VocabParallelEmbedding (embed_tokens).

Stock 0.28.0 only hands AutoGPTQ to LinearBase and ParallelLMHead. embed_tokens
therefore stays UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod and crashes if the checkpoint has
qweight instead of .weight. Three hunks:

  1. INCConfig.get_quant_method — also dispatch a quantized
     VocabParallelEmbedding (exact type, not ParallelLMHead).
  2. INCLinearMethod.embedding — dequant-on-gather over the GPTQ layout.
  3. Skip Marlin repack for that layer so the gather still sees qweight
     packed along the input dim.

lm_head is unchanged (ParallelLMHead still goes through Marlin GEMM).

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/inc-gptq-embed.patch

Validated against vLLM 0.28.0. Reapply after upgrades.

--- a/model_executor/layers/quantization/inc/inc_linear.py
+++ b/model_executor/layers/quantization/inc/inc_linear.py
@@ -45,3 +45,23 @@
         bias: torch.Tensor | None = None,
     ) -> torch.Tensor:
         return self.scheme.apply_weights(layer, x, bias)
+
+    def embedding(self, layer: torch.nn.Module, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        # syv: dequant-on-gather for a GPTQ-packed vocab table. Marlin repack
+        # is skipped for VocabParallelEmbedding (inc_wna16_linear.py), so
+        # qweight is still [K/pack, V].
+        cfg = getattr(self.scheme, "layer_config", None)
+        bits = getattr(cfg, "bits", 8)
+        group = getattr(cfg, "group_size", 128)
+        pack = 32 // bits
+        zp = 1 << (bits - 1)
+        maxq = (1 << bits) - 1
+        ids = x.reshape(-1)
+        qw = layer.qweight.index_select(1, ids)
+        sc = layer.scales.index_select(1, ids).float()
+        shifts = torch.arange(pack, device=qw.device, dtype=torch.int32) * bits
+        q = (
+            (qw.unsqueeze(1) >> shifts.view(1, pack, 1)) & maxq
+        ).reshape(-1, ids.numel()).float() - zp
+        w = (q * sc.repeat_interleave(group, dim=0)).to(layer.scales.dtype)
+        return w.t().reshape(*x.shape, -1)
